  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kallol Benerjee vs State (U.T. Chandigarh), Through Food ... on 21 August, 2024 Author: Rajesh Bhardwaj Bench: Rajesh Bhardwaj Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:107123 Crm-M-37550-2024 -1- 121 In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana At Chandigarh Crm-M-37550-2024 Date of Decision: 21.08.2024 Kallol Banerjee ..... Petitioner Versus State of Ut Chandigarh .......Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rajesh Bhardwaj Present: Mr. Arshdeep Singh Cheema, Advocate, for the petitioner.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "He submits that thus, prosecution of the petitioner is in Kallol Benerjee vs State (U.T. Chandigarh), Through Food ... on 21 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84881091/ 1 violation of the set norms under the law. 3. Notice of motion. 4. However, learned counsel for the petitioner has submitted that Vijay Kumar had no authority to make a statement before the Court as is reflected in the order. After hearing learned counsel for the petitioner and perusing the record, it is apparent that person nominated for day to day affair of the company is Bipul Jha and thus, prosecution of the petitioner is not as per law."
  },
